WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.480
What the hell is this?!

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.340
We have all these fines

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:11.840
for unauthorized magic use that wasn't adjudged
to be fair use under article 10, Cecil!

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.490
You could buy an expensive car
with that money.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.820
Don't act like it's someone else's problem!

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.680
This is all your fault!

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:21.220
We also have these, Cecil.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.740
In accordance with
magic-prohibition law, article 5:

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:30.000
Once a wizard's magical powers
awaken, that person,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.760
or their legal guardian,
must immediately register them.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.010
You didn't do that, right?

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:39.010
We got fined.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.080
...I'll work hard to repay you for—

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.270
That isn't the problem here!

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:50.280
It's the fact that whenever any little
problem arises, you resort to using magic!

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.670
...B-But...

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:54.380
Whether I was catching
a robber or getting attacked.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.890
They were situations where I had to
use magic to resolve the situation.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.280
Wasn't it the same for you, Hachimitsu?

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.040
Are you in a position to
talk about anyone else?

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:10.290
You always blame others instead
of realizing your own mistakes.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:11.800
...But...

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.300
If you can't resolve a case without resorting
to magic, then you're useless as a lawyer.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.470
Do you understand?

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.470
I know I have a lot to learn,

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:21.810
but I'm not useless!

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.810
That's exactly the arrogant
attitude I'm talking about!

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:29.770
Changing the topic, are we?

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:32.700
Don't be mean to Cecilun, Natcchi!

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:33.760
Yeah.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.780
I know you're sexually frustrated,
...considering you're not getting any, but...

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:39.780
That's sexual harassment, Sasori.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.530
Oh, do you actually have a man?

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.540
That's none of your business.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:50.380
At any rate, we live and die by the law.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.920
At times, it's a reliable companion. However,
other times, it's an obstacle we need to overcome.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:58.260
I think you've experienced
that firsthand, Cecil.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.190
I know you're doing your best,

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:06.320
but every now and then, you should
take a moment to look around you.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:08.180
What do you see?

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:10.300
Just the agency in debt!

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.720
And a number of complaints.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.480
Don't give up, Sudou.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.840
I didn't <i>want to use magic, you know.</i>

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:26.740
It may have been out of your hands,
but it's still causing trouble for the agency.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:32.150
I wish my magic would just disappear.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:33.320
...Cecilcchi...

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:39.920
Don't worry about what happened today.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:43.680
Your smile always makes me
feel better, Tsunomin.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.680
I'll give you another
chance to feel better!

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.920
Tomorrow's Saturday,
so hang out with me.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:48.980
What's going on?

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.940
...Oh, just a transformation...

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:53.940
A transformation?

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:59.660
Sasorin said that you've got meat
...in all the right places, Cecilcchi...

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:00.950
I'm sure it'll look good.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:03.280
Sheesh.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.040
Can't Sori see anyone
in a non-pervy way?

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:08.450
So, what do you want me to do?

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:10.710
You'll just have to wait and see.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.520
Meet me tomorrow
in Kourakuen at 1 PM.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:15.460
...Oh, um...

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.460
Tsunomi is rather pushy.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.070
...I didn't even agree to go...

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.160
What's this?

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:28.970
I will carry my indomitable hope into the dark night

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:28.970
yami no naka no shinjitsu ga hikari kagayaku you ni

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:35.270
so that it may light a shining fire of truth there

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:35.270
kagi no nai kibou wo tokihanatou

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:50.740
I was born bleeding from my hands,

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:50.740
naze te no hira no kizu wo daite umareochita imi

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:54.730
and why was I born not a thousand years in the past or the future,

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:54.730
sennen kako demo mirai demo naku

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.040
but in the present?

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.040
erabareta ima

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.390
The scales of justice are fragile

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.390
zen'aku hakaru tenbin wa zeijaku

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:05.450
The waning, waxing moon calls to a flower on the earth

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:05.450
michikakeru tsuki ga izanau gisei no chi ni saita

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.350
the color of blood

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.350
chi no iro no hana

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.850
I will give all I have

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.850
tatta hitotsu kanau nara

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:12.550
if it means one of my wishes will come true

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:12.550
subete wo sasageyou

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:15.830
I have a "post nubila phoebus" kind of personality

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:15.830
post nubila phoebus kokoro

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.680
which I will show the world

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.680
kaze ni hanatte

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:20.680
I want to slash apart the curtain of raven black,

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:20.680
shikkoku no curtain hikichigiri

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:23.370
and look at a new world

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:23.370
chigau sora wo mitemitai

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:26.040
My love stabs at the cracks

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:26.040
sabita unmei no hibiware

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:28.510
of a stagnant fate

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:28.510
omoi wa nejikonde

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:31.370
No matter how long the storm lasts,

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:31.370
donnani arasoi tsuzuketemo

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:33.980
time itself will not stop breathing

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:33.980
toki wa kokyuu wo yamenai

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.740
What remains after destruction, rebirth,

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.740
kowashite tsunde kowashite

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:39.220
and further destruction?

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:39.220
nani ga nokoru darou

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:41.950
I'm sure I can put an end to a thousand nights of doubt

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:41.950
sou nanajuuokuban no mayoi mo

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:45.100
and to the system of the world

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:45.100
sono haichizu wa kakikaerareru

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.780
I'm sure that one day I will find a place where I can shine

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.780
moetsukitemo kagayakeru basho e

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:52.030
even if only ashes will remain

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:52.030
itsuka tadoritsukeru

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:00.530
Case 6

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:00.530
Hero Show

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.910
Oh, now you've gone and done it.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.050
We're pretty close.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.360
No entry?

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:24.630
...No sense of direction...

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:25.930
Shut up!

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.230
Sheesh, I don't get it!

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:31.290
I told you that you've got
no sense of direction.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:33.690
How about you drive then, Nana Genie?

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.940
What was that?

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.700
A metamoloid!

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.870
Something's happening!

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.930
Let's go, Nana Genie.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.110
Is everyone okay?

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:03.970
...Let go...

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:05.220
Ow!

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:09.770
You can't go shooting off
...a rocket launcher in the city...

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:10.970
This isn't the time!

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:15.230
Where on Earth did you
get a SMAW launcher, anyway?

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:17.570
I have my sources.

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:21.230
Do you really think normal police gear
is enough to fight wizards?

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:26.990
Come any closer, and we'll kill her.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.150
What the hell is she doing here?!

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:32.240
...Cecil...

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.560
She's late.

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:36.750
...Jeez...

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:40.250
What are you doing, Cecilcchi?

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:44.760
There's a ninety-three-percent
chance she won't come.

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:47.760
I bet she's just ignoring you.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.770
I won't allow sudden cancellations.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:58.270
<i>The suspects have barricaded
themselves in a cram school</i>

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:02.010
<i>and declared themselves as part of the
wizard terrorist group, Gumegoma.</i>

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:05.650
<i>And after attacking the Metropolitan
Police Department and National Police Agency,</i>

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:08.030
<i>it appears they have taken
four children, a teacher,</i>

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:15.000
<i>and one teenage girl, who had
just been passing by, hostage.</i>

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:19.670
<i>The suspects have not made
any demands as of yet,</i>

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.880
<i>and there is concern
for the hostages' safety.</i>

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.180
...Cecilun...

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.450
SAT is in position.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.010
They can enter on your mark.

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.090
I'll make the call.

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:39.190
I don't want this to be a long fight.

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:41.340
A raid would be too dangerous.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:42.690
We should explore other options.

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:46.970
They're a part of a violent,
armed Wud group.

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:49.040
There are children inside.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:51.080
Their safety comes first!

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.470
In cases like these,

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:56.860
the longer we sit and wait for
their move, the worse things get.

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:58.520
...Cecil's in there...

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:00.360
If all else fails,
...I'm sure she'll be able to—

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:00.960
Shizumu!

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.090
She may be a Wud, but she's a civilian!

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:05.210
Do you understand?

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:06.760
Self-control will guarantee exam success.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:06.760
Cultivate willpower that is immune to luck.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.860
When can we leave?

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:12.900
I dunno.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:16.720
D-Don't worry, everyone.
I'll keep you safe.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:17.770
Thanks!

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:21.310
Hey, who's that girl?

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:30.360
Why don't you use
your magic to beat them?

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.760
They'll shoot us if we try anything.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.420
At this rate, I can't undo
my seals to use magic.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:42.370
If you can't resolve a case without resorting
to magic, then you're useless as a lawyer.

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:45.700
Excuse me!

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.050
What?

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:50.610
My name is Sudou Cecil.
I'm a wizard barrister.

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.260
Why are you doing this?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.490
Huh?

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.740
If there's a police raid,

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:00.110
then you might not make it out alive.

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:02.720
So can you at least release the children?

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:04.460
You want to know why we're doing this?

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:06.400
Yes!

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:09.150
I'll fill you in.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:11.390
...Our motive is...

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:16.160
world conquest!

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.910
World... conquest?

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:26.170
Good and evil, light and dark,
exist together in this world.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:29.670
It's the same in both
human and wizard worlds.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:33.430
But the time for shadow
to overcome light is now!

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:37.550
And we, the world's most ruthless
and evil criminal organization, Gumegoma,

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:41.030
will be the ones to do it!

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.450
Cecil, was it?

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:52.610
You should be honored to be
part of our plan to conquer the world.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.490
Wh-What the heck?

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:58.580
They're idiots.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:01.670
That sounds like something
Chiccho Dente would say.

00:10:01.670 --> 00:10:02.330
How lame.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:07.230
Hopefully, some heroes like
...the Agurangers will save us...

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:09.930
...But reality isn't like TV...

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:17.330
<i>There's something off about these guys.</i>

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:28.690
The time for shadow to
overcome light is now!

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.800
Dente, over here!

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:31.860
Chiccho!

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.360
Transform!

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:38.360
Bambi Red, Bambina, has arrived!

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:41.690
Get knocked out by the red of justice!

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.750
Hey, someone's barricaded
themselves in some building.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.290
Mag Terrorists Barricade themselves inside School!

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.050
It's the cram school on the
third block of Hongou.

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:49.290
That's not too far from here.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.250
They've taken women
...and children hostage...

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:52.470
Shit.

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:53.380
You wanna go look?

00:10:55.260 --> 00:11:00.250
Bambi Red won't stand for someone who
takes helpless women and children hostage!

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:01.830
Curse you, Chiccho Dente!

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:05.520
I'll shatter your evil plans
with my kick of justice!

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:08.230
Sorry, are you okay?

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.010
Yeah.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:13.990
There she goes again...

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:17.030
She has no chance of stopping them!

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:22.230
...I'm hungry...

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:24.540
I wanna go home.

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:27.190
It'll only be a little longer, everyone.

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:29.540
The police will come and save us.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:30.610
Okay!

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:32.040
Okay.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:37.050
If worse comes to worst,
...I'll risk my life to protect you...

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:40.550
Are you okay, Miss?

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:43.370
Y-Yeah.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.600
Thanks for asking.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:46.690
Oh, right.

00:11:46.690 --> 00:11:48.930
I think I have some snacks in my bag.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.690
So if you guys get hungry, help yourselves.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:54.440
Yay! Thanks, Miss!

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:58.570
Hey, it's Agurangers!

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:00.570
Agurangers?

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:03.410
<i>Maiden Force Agurangers.</i>

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:06.350
It's a super popular TV show.
Haven't you heard of it?

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:09.580
...I haven't watched TV in years, so...

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:12.990
This is Bambi Pink!

00:12:12.990 --> 00:12:14.790
Try it on, Miss.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:16.750
She's a heroine of justice.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:19.090
I'll tell you her catchphrase and pose!

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:21.030
Huh? Like, right now?!

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:22.590
No way, no way, no way, no way!

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:32.020
Do it.

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:37.900
B-Bambi Pink has arrived!

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:41.550
...I'll take out evil with the pink of justice...

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:46.770
That's pretty hot.

00:12:46.770 --> 00:12:48.660
She's got meat in all the right places.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:52.980
You really look cute, Miss!

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:54.420
Yeah, it's really nice.

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:56.920
Y-You think so?

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.170
...Super pervy...

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:02.670
You should go to the Court
for Magic dressed like that.

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:04.170
Shut up!

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.680
What are the suspects' demands?

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.730
They haven't made any yet.

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:11.060
How long do those bastards
plan to stay in there?

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:13.190
What an unlucky day.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:16.330
We're sending a small camera
into the classroom.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:18.310
Get in position to infiltrate.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:19.270
Understood.

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:22.320
Do you plan on going in?

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:24.210
I'm in charge here.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:26.210
Stop trying to butt in, Shizumu.

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:28.430
People will die if you rush things.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:31.290
Please consider getting
the hostages out safely first!

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:32.490
What the hell is with you?

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.580
Do you want to be in charge instead?

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:38.340
I'm just worried about
the children and Cecil.

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:41.490
You've been mentioning
...Cecil over and over...

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:48.100
Hey, get away from there!

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:49.460
What the hell is that?

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:50.790
Rather, <i>who the hell is that?</i>

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:53.400
<i>Maiden Force Agurangers?</i>

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.600
What the hell is that?

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:57.170
The heroine of justice, Bambi Red,

00:13:57.170 --> 00:14:00.160
was about to face
Chiccho Dente alone.

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:01.610
Go forth, Bambi Red.

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:04.700
Bambi Red has arrived!

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:07.610
Get knocked down by the red of justice!

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:09.530
...What the—

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:10.700
Bambi Red!

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.530
Minions of evil!

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:16.230
I, Bambi Red, shall take care of all of you!

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:17.210
Prepare yourselves!

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:20.840
Take that! The whip of justice!

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.910
<i>Bambi Kick!</i>

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:26.970
Justice will prevail.

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:28.840
Huh?

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:32.830
You're kidding.
...This wasn't supposed to happen...

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:35.410
Tsunomin, use your magic.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:42.230
Huh? Cecilcchi?

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:45.250
Act like a hero all you want,
but could you at least win?

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:49.240
She's just doing her best
to act like Bambi Red.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:51.740
You need to discipline her more.

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:54.290
This is really odd.

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:55.000
What?

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.550
They've been acting odd
for a while now.

00:14:58.550 --> 00:15:02.320
I don't think they plan on
harming the hostages at all.

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:04.500
What do you mean?

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:08.550
They haven't done anything
...to the children or the teacher...

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:11.210
Hey, why aren't you using your magic?

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:14.950
Because they were pointing a gun
...at me for the longest time...

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:18.550
Tsunomin, why didn't
you use magic, either?

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:21.190
Because Bambi Red
doesn't use magic.

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:22.520
Would you quit the act already?!

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:26.620
If they show any intent of
...harming the kids, though...

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:29.210
<i>Then we'll use our magic.</i>

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:32.620
Your opportunity is right before you.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:36.690
It's nearly show time.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:39.210
Engage!

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:56.470
Everyone, head toward the exit!

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:58.720
Hurry and take the children.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:01.980
Out of my way!

00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:11.130
...Human adults are sickening...

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:12.610
How could you do that
in front of the children?!

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:17.870
You're next.

00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:19.370
Cecilcchi!

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:41.270
We're almost there, Cecilun.

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:50.900
...What the heck...

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.180
...What—

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:53.930
You little!

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:57.830
<i>Gumegoma Metamoloid... go!</i>

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:16.260
Keiji!

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:18.260
It's a diaboloid!

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.770
You have my permission!

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:21.050
...Assistant Inspector Shizumu...

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:22.270
Cecil!

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:27.390
<i>Cecil Diaboloid, go!</i>

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:09.170
Are you hurt?

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:12.650
S-So cool!

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:15.450
Wow! It's a magical robot!

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:16.810
All right.

00:18:16.810 --> 00:18:18.200
I guess I'll go too.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.830
You're amazing, Miss!

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.670
Just like a real hero.

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:51.570
You're not getting away!

00:18:57.240 --> 00:19:00.260
...So you guys were heroes...

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:01.910
Magic is awesome!

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:04.330
Do you think we'll be
able to use it someday too?

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:07.410
Can humans become
wizards someday too?

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:10.920
Keiji!

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:11.540
Seira!

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:12.840
Dad!

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:15.040
Thanks so much!

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:15.800
Bye!

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:22.660
When you're a kid, being
human or Wud doesn't matter.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:24.400
Yeah.

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:36.570
Freeze!

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:42.820
As requested, we made Sudou Cecil's
magic awaken again, Shizumu.

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:45.950
Yeah.

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:52.610
Have you given any more thought
to making us leaders of Macal?

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:56.290
You wouldn't want everyone to know
that you're actually a Wud, would you?

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:59.370
You know wizards can't
...work as public servants...

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:02.630
So how will you maintain
your position as a police officer?

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:05.890
No one will find out.

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:19.320
...Shizumu...

00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:22.990
They resisted, so I shot them.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:29.870
Hand over your gun.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.010
Butterfly Law Offices

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:41.380
You used magic again?!

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:43.510
Yes.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:47.130
Sudou is always getting
dragged into strange incidents.

00:20:47.130 --> 00:20:48.310
It's true.

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:51.770
For some reason, things get worse
whenever Cecil's involved.

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:56.020
But we're the heroes
who helped the kids.

00:20:56.670 --> 00:20:59.280
...You can take the fine out of my pay...

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:05.280
A "Magic Use" permit?

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:06.380
Huh?

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:11.870
"Applicant: Ekusou Shizumu"?

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.310
Ekusou Shizumu

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.310
User:

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.310
Sudou Cecil

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.310
Applicant:

00:21:10.310 --> 00:21:12.290
Ekusou Shizumu

00:21:10.310 --> 00:21:12.290
Sudou Cecil

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:13.610
...This is...

00:21:13.610 --> 00:21:17.290
Assistant Inspector Shizumu
...submitted the application himself...

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:21.920
Since it's been adjudged to
be fair use, there is no fine.

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:23.550
Really?

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:27.710
I'll overlook it this time,
but don't expect this to always be the case.

00:21:27.710 --> 00:21:28.930
Understood?

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:30.120
Yes, sir!

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:34.310
Looks like justice prevailed, huh?

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:36.560
Yep!

00:21:37.300 --> 00:21:39.720
You're all so naïve!

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:43.890
Kokki, something was weird.

00:21:43.890 --> 00:21:45.110
What do you mean?

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:50.330
I felt like there was some magic
at work besides Cecil and Tsunomi's.

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:51.890
...I agree...

00:21:51.890 --> 00:21:54.450
Something only we
...familiars would sense...

00:21:55.190 --> 00:21:57.550
Maybe it's Cecil's dormant magic?

00:21:57.550 --> 00:22:01.090
...No, it's something else...

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:04.090
Let's cosplay again, Cecilcchi.

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:05.310
I wanna see!

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:07.330
Show me in person, Cecilcchi!

00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:09.230
I'll never show you, Sori!

00:22:25.900 --> 00:22:32.830
My heart may cry silently,

00:22:25.900 --> 00:22:32.830
kokoro ga donna ni namida afuretemo

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:40.420
but I still want to behold the blue sky

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:40.420
hitomi ni aozora utsushiteitai

00:22:40.660 --> 00:22:47.990
I want to have something like the strength of flowers

00:22:40.660 --> 00:22:47.990
concrete-iro no machi no katasumi ni

00:22:47.990 --> 00:22:55.400
which bloom in the nooks of the endless concrete of the city

00:22:47.990 --> 00:22:55.400
sotto saku hana no tsuyosa wo manetai

00:22:55.400 --> 00:23:02.810
Starting today, I won't try to wriggle out by saying

00:22:55.400 --> 00:23:02.810
maegami ga jama de mienai nante iiwake

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:06.630
that I saw nothing because my hair was in the way

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:06.630
kyou kara shinai

00:23:07.580 --> 00:23:15.070
Beyond the horizon, my future awaits me,

00:23:07.580 --> 00:23:15.070
chiheisen no mukou ni ashita ga matteru kara

00:23:15.070 --> 00:23:20.290
so I will let the sun in my heart

00:23:15.070 --> 00:23:20.290
kono mune no hitotsu no taiyou

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:22.340
shine out far and wide

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:22.340
tooku hanatte

00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:29.710
I will overtake the earth's rotation on the path I walk,

00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:29.710
chikyuu no jiten wo oikosu kurai hitamuki ni arukou

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:37.800
with trusting love inside my heart

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:37.800
shinjiru omoi dakishimete doko made mo
